    "alert_id": "EFV_AMLODIPINE_INTERACTION_004",
    "title": "Efavirenz may lower amlodipine levels; BP uncontrolled",
    "message": "Guidelines note that efavirenz can potentially decrease dihydropyridine (amlodipine, nifedipine) drug levels, though no dose adjustments are required. Patient on EFV with amlodipine 5 mg has BP 146/94 today, suboptimally controlled. Contributing factors include missed amlodipine doses while travelling. The interaction may partly reduce antihypertensive efficacy, but adherence is the more likely dominant cause. Guidelines also list amlodipine side effects including lower limb oedema, headache, and palpitations; patient has no pedal oedema today.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "low",
    "recommended_action": "Reinforce amlodipine adherence; if BP remains above target despite full adherence, uptitrate or add a second antihypertensive per guidelines.",
